<title>UK: UK unemployment falls 67,800 in Jan.</title>
<headline>UK unemployment falls 67,800 in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics released the following provisional data for unemployment in January. (Previous estimates for December in brackets, minus denotes fall, data seasonally adjusted unless indicated)</p>
<p>    UNEMPLOYMENT		    JAN	 DEC     (PREL DEC)</p>
<p>    Monthly change		-67,800   -46,700   (-45,100)</p>
<p>    Rate (pct)			6.5	 6.7	   (6.7)</p>
<p>    Monthly non-s/adj change  +39,600     n/a	(-3,200)</p>
<p>    Monthly non-s/adj rate	6.8	 6.7	   (6.7)</p>
<p>NOTE - Consensus forecast was for seasonally adjusted fall of 30,000 in January.  </p>
<p>    Unemployment level (million)   1,815	1,883    (1,884.7)</p>
<p>    Unemployment level unadj   1,908	1,868    (1,868.2)</p>
<p>    Avg change in past 3m     -70,000    -62,600   (-62,000)</p>
<p>    Avg change in past 6m     -51,800    -44,500   (-44,300)</p>
<p>   AVERAGE EARNINGS			DEC	NOV (PREL NOV)</p>
<p>   underlying yearly chng (pct)	4.25     4.25    (4.00)</p>
<p>   index (base 1990)		     135.2    134.2   (134.2)</p>
<p>   actual yearly chng (pct)		4.5     4.0     (4.0)</p>
<p>By sector (annual pct chng)</p>
<p>   Production-- underlying		 4.75     4.5   (4.25)</p>
<p>		 -- actual		     4.9	4.5    (4.5)</p>
<p>    Manufacturing -- underlying	  4.75     4.5    (4.5)</p>
<p>			-- actual		4.8	4.7    (4.7)</p>
<p>    Services -- underlying		 4.0	4.0   (3.75)</p>
<p>		 -- actual		     4.5	3.6    (3.6)</p>
<p>NOTE: consensus forecast 4.00 pct for overall underlying average earnings.</p>
<p>    UNIT WAGE COSTS	    Dec	   Nov</p>
<p>    Monthly change vs yr ago 2.4	   3.7   (4.1)</p>
<p>    Index (base=1990)	  115.5	114.8  (115.3)</p>
<p>    3-mth versus same yr/ago 3.2	  4.0    (4.2)</p>
<p>    Index (base=1990)	  114.8	114.5 (114.8)</p>
<p>PRODUCTIVITY</p>
<p>    monthly change vs yr ago 2.4	   0.9  (+0.5)</p>
<p>    Index (base=1990)	  122.2	 121.8 (121.4)</p>
<p>    3mth vs same year ago    1.3	   0.5  (+0.3)</p>
<p>    Index (base=1990)	  122.0	 121.7 (121.4)</p>
<p>OVERALL EMPLOYMENT (THOUSANDS, S/ADJ)</p>
<p>    EMPLOYEES IN EMPLOYMENT	   Q3	 Q2     Q3 95</p>
<p>    LEVEL				   22,293 22,183   21,996</p>
<p>    CHANGE				   +110    +59	+13</p>
<p>    WORKFORCE IN EMPLOYMENT	   26,076 25,876   25,776</p>
<p>						 +200    +12	-7</p>
<p>    JOB CENTRE VACANCIES		JAN	  DEC</p>
<p>    change				 -3,500     -2,400 (-1,200)</p>
<p>    level				  262,800   266,300</p>
<p>    Avg 3m change			   +100     +4,200 (+4,600)</p>
<p>The ONS said January boasted the lowest rate of claimant unemployment since 1990 with the seasonally adjusted unemployment rate is at its lowest level since December 1990.</p>
<p>The change in the claimant count was exaggerated by an estimate 3,000 in January due to backlogs caused by the jobseekers allowance. Manufacturing employment fell be 4,000 in December, the ONS said.  </p>
<p>Overall average earnings growth, up 4.25%, is at its highest level since February 1993.</p>
<p>Average earnings in the manufacturing industry are growing at their highest level since May 1995. Earnings growth in the production industry is at its highest since July 1995.</p>
